schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Token-Based Coordination Mechanisms
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    The set of mechanisms (signaling, voting, reputation, incentives/penalties)
    by which token-holding groups align on priorities and manage shared
    resources without a single central decision-maker.
  source_traditions:
    - DAO governance tooling (Snapshot signaling, Tally on-chain voting)
    - reputation-based contribution tracking (Colony)
    - quadratic funding mechanism design (Gitcoin)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used in the article to frame tokens as a governance/coordination layer
    for regenerative communities, distinct from tokens as speculative assets.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - token-weighted voting (plutocratic variant)
    - reputation/non-transferable Soulbound Tokens (SBTs) as an alternative to wealth-based influence
  important_distinctions:
    - signaling (non-binding temperature check) vs voting (binding decision)
    - on-chain voting (permanent record, gas cost) vs off-chain voting (lighter weight, e.g. Snapshot)
    - token-wealth-based influence vs contribution/reputation-based influence
  tensions:
    - decentralized framing vs multisig-concentrated real power
    - rewarding participation vs penalizing inactivity without excluding low-capacity members
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating "tokens for coordination" as a single solved pattern risks hiding
    that most implementations still concentrate power in early/wealthy holders
    or small multisig groups — the article names this explicitly as a
    recurring, unsolved problem across "thousands of DAOs."
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/tokens-coordination-tools.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  source_lineage: tokens-coordination-tools.md
